/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The CPI Trend Over Time graph \(1960-2024\) illustrates a steady rise in the Consumer Price Index, reflecting increasing costs of goods and services over the decades. Notable surges in CPI coincide with major economic events, such as the 1970s oil crisis and the 1991 economic reforms. In recent years, the trend shows a more gradual increase, indicating better inflation control and economic stability. This upward trajectory highlights the importance of CPI as a measure of inflation and its impact on the cost of living and purchasing power.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
